{"questions":[{"question_id":"1ky3yym7r","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"physics","chapter":"rotational-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"combined-translational-and-rotational-motion","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"a-uniform-circular-disc-of-mass-15-kg-and-radius-05-m-is-i-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-bi6tiaysnnjlbtnv","content":"A uniform circular disc of mass 1.5 kg and radius 0.5 m is initially at rest on a horizontal frictionless surface. Three forces of equal magnitude F = 0.5 N are applied simultaneously along the three sides of an equilateral triangle XYZ with its vertices on the perimeter of the disc (see figure). One second after applying the forces, the angular speed of the disc in rad s<sup>-1</sup> is<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc-11ec-bb8f-b3be3f2269a8/file-1ky4no491.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc-11ec-bb8f-b3be3f2269a8/file-1ky4no491.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Rotational Motion Question 46 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc-11ec-bb8f-b3be3f2269a8/file-1ky4no491.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc-11ec-bb8f-b3be3f2269a8/file-1ky4no491.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc-11ec-bb8f-b3be3f2269a8/file-1ky4no491.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1ky4no490/72af5be2-e0b4-4c9b-bdbb-16cb903c79e1/e2788440-6fdc